<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
<p class="font-bold">Same gap in the launch frame does not mean an unstretched string.</p>
<svg viewBox="0 0 480 225" class="w-full" role="img" aria-labelledby="bell-fig-title bell-fig-desc">
<title id="bell-fig-title">Two equally accelerating ships with a string stretched between them</title><desc id="bell-fig-desc">Before and after accelerating in the launch frame, the ships have the same separation. The gap exceeds the length that a freely moving, unstretched string would occupy at their new speed.</desc>
<g fill="currentColor" font-size="18"><text x="14" y="28">Before acceleration</text><text x="14" y="139">After acceleration</text></g>
<g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
<rect x="80" y="49" width="46" height="28" fill="#387a91"/><rect x="317" y="49" width="46" height="28" fill="#387a91"/><path d="M126 63 H317" stroke="#d7a13d" stroke-width="5"/>
<rect x="80" y="160" width="46" height="28" fill="#387a91"/><rect x="317" y="160" width="46" height="28" fill="#387a91"/><path d="M126 174 H317" stroke="#bd4b37" stroke-width="5"/>
</g>
<g fill="currentColor" font-size="16" text-anchor="middle"><text x="223" y="45">fixed distance in launch frame</text><text x="223" y="212">moving string is stretched</text></g>
<g fill="currentColor" font-size="27"><text x="382" y="76">→</text><text x="382" y="186">→→</text></g>
</svg>
<figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">Both ships gain speed in exactly the same way, so their separation stays fixed as measured at launch. Yet an unstretched string moving at their new speed would occupy a shorter length in that frame. It is stretched and may break. The arrows and positions are schematic.</figcaption></figure>